The application will be available at `http://localhost:5000` (development) or `http://localhost:8000` (production).

### Project Structure

## Deployment

```

pulse-of-humanity/### Environment Variables for Production

├── app.py                 # Main Flask application

├── requirements.txt       # Python dependenciesSet the following environment variables in your production environment:

├── render.yaml           # Render deployment config

├── gunicorn.conf.py      # Production server config- `SECRET_KEY`: Strong secret key for Flask sessions

├── .env.example          # Environment variables template- `FLASK_ENV`: Set to `production`

├── validate_env.py       # Environment validation script- `SMTP_SERVER`: Your SMTP server hostname

├── security_audit.py     # Security audit script- `SMTP_PORT`: SMTP port (usually 587 for TLS)

└── docs/                # Documentation- `SMTP_USERNAME`: Your SMTP username

    ├── DEPLOYMENT.md     # Deployment guide- `SMTP_PASSWORD`: Your SMTP password or app-specific password

    └── MOBILE_RESPONSIVENESS_REPORT.md- `SMTP_FROM_EMAIL`: From email address

```- `CONTACT_TO_EMAIL`: Email address to receive contact form submissions



